---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;
// TEMPLATE TEXT — have it reviewed for your business and jurisdiction before launch.
const updated = '2026-01-01';
const L = site.legal;
---

<Base title="Terms of service" description={`Terms of service for ${site.brandName} travel eSIMs.`}>
  <article class="container-page prose-page py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>
      These terms apply to eSIM data plans sold on {site.websiteUrl.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')} by {L.companyName}, {L.address}{L.registration ? ` (${L.registration})` : ''}
      ("we", "us"). By buying a plan you agree to them.
    </p>

    <h2>1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      We sell prepaid, data-only eSIM plans for use abroad. Each plan has a data allowance (or a daily allowance) and a validity period, shown before you buy.
      The validity period starts when the eSIM first connects to a supported network in a covered country, unless the plan page says otherwise.
      Plans do not include a phone number, calls or SMS.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your device</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for checking that your device supports eSIM and is not locked to a carrier before you buy (see <a href="/compatibility">compatibility</a>).
      Coverage, speed and availability depend on local partner networks and may vary.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Prices and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are shown in US dollars and are charged at checkout through Stripe. Your bank may apply currency conversion fees. We may change prices at any time;
      the price you pay is the one shown at checkout.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Delivery</h2>
    <p>
      Your eSIM (QR code and installation details) is shown on screen after payment and sent to the email address you provide, normally within minutes.
      Keep the QR code private: anyone with it can install your plan.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Refunds</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If your eSIM has not been installed, you may request a refund within 30 days of purchase.</li>
      <li>If the eSIM cannot be installed or does not connect because of a fault on our side, we will replace it or refund you.</li>
      <li>Once an eSIM has been installed or has used data, it cannot be refunded, except where required by law.</li>
      <li>Unused data or days are not refundable after the plan has started.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To request a refund write to <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with your order number.</p>

    <h2>6. Fair use</h2>
    <p>Plans are for personal use while travelling. Use for illegal purposes, network abuse or resale is not allowed, and we may suspend plans that are misused.</p>

    <h2>7. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, our liability for any claim relating to a plan is limited to the price you paid for it. Nothing in these terms limits rights
      you have under consumer protection law.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of {L.jurisdiction}. Mandatory consumer protections of your country of residence still apply.</p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>{L.companyName}, {L.address}. Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
